        "question_text": "<p>Which wood joint is most suitable for <b>connecting two pieces of wood at a right angle</b> while providing maximum strength?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The <b>mortise and tenon joint</b> is one of the strongest joints for connecting two pieces of wood at a right angle. It consists of a <i>tenon</i> (projection) on one piece that fits into a <i>mortise</i> (hole) on the other, providing excellent resistance to racking and pulling forces. Other joints like <i>dovetail</i> or <i>dowel</i> are strong but may not offer the same level of structural integrity for all applications.</p>",
